		)
		(uuid "cff877c1-1508-4873-83ab-1b19c462b053")
	)
	(text "The two pins Ver_1 and Ver_2 allow the host board/MCU to detect \nwhat type and version of communication board is connected.\nEach Ver_1/2 pin has a 40.2k resistor to GND on the host side, and \nthe resisitor loaded on the Cicada dagughter board (this PCB) \ncreates a voltage divider that is then read by the host MCU as an \nanalog voltage\n\nThe Ver_1 pin describes the type of Cicada comms board \n(eg 2G, 3G/4G, WIFI etc) and the Ver_2 pin is the release version \nof the Cicada PCB/BOM (as relevant to the host HW/FW).\n\nSee the table for the resistor -> version number relationship. Note \nthat the resistor of this board is the R_Bottom\n\nNote that these version resistors only code for version changes \nthat are relevant for FW or need to be tracked remotely. The full \npart release version (eg P-1000101-V1.0.0) may increment without \ntriggering a version resistor change"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 497.078 69.8246 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "d8304b54-8642-4e73-9927-c39416a86441")
	)
	(text "800mA"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 208.915 168.91 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.7272 1.7272)
				(thickness 0.3454)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "e3204e10-66e3-43cf-8272-8621a16a544a")
	)
	(text "2"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 498.983 90.1446 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1938 1.1938)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "e53917a3-92f9-469d-a47a-101522b0302f")
	)
	(text "We use a 2x10 female pin socket as it fits perfectly in a 2x8\nshrouded pin header on the host side. We don't use a 2x8 \npin socket as it is narrower than a 2x8 shrouded header \nand can allowing off-by-1 pin insertion. We don't use a 2x8 \nkeyed pin sockets are they seem to be very uncommon."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 415.163 44.4246 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.4986 1.4986)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "e7512d6a-3a77-45fa-9913-f60a9f972df2")
	)
